    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52731" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιστεῖον</span></b> , τό,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιστεύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>offering of what is fairest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				23
			</span></i>: pl., name of a festival and <i>beauty-contest</i> at
			Lesbos, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.129
			</span></i>: in pl. also, <i>the fairest prize</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πρῶτα κ. ἀριστεύσας στρατοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					435
				</span></i>
			 (cf. Sch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν φαλύρων τὰ
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				56.9
			</span></i> (Argos, <span class="entity">v B. C.</span>); so in sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(9).189.36
			</span></i> (Eretria, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				207.19
			</span></i> (ibid., <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>beautyprize</i>, of the apple of Paris, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				20.1
			</span></i>.</div>
